<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>FAQ - Verify My Collectible</title>
  <style>
    * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: #333;
      background: #f9fafb;
    }
    .container {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 40px 20px;
      background: white;
      min-height: 100vh;
    }
    h1 {
      color: #1a1a1a;
      margin-bottom: 30px;
      font-size: 32px;
    }
    .faq-item {
      margin-bottom: 30px;
      padding-bottom: 30px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    }
    .faq-item:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
    }
    .question {
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: #1a1a1a;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    .answer {
      color: #4a4a4a;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .answer ul {
      margin-left: 20px;
      margin-top: 10px;
    }
    .answer li {
      margin-bottom: 5px;
    }
    .contact-box {
      margin-top: 40px;
      padding: 20px;
      background: #f0f9ff;
      border-radius: 8px;
      border-left: 4px solid #3b82f6;
    }
    .contact-box h2 {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      color: #1a1a1a;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">What is Verify My Collectible?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        Verify My Collectible is a Shopify app that helps you manage and authenticate your collectible inventory. It allows you to create categories, add items with serial numbers and images, and provide a verification system for your customers to confirm the authenticity of their collectibles.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">How do I install the app?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        <ul>
          <li>Find Verify My Collectible in the Shopify App Store</li>
          <li>Click "Add app" and approve the permissions</li>
          <li>Choose a subscription plan that fits your needs</li>
          <li>Start adding your collectible categories and items</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">What subscription plans are available?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        We offer three plans:
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Basic ($9.99/month):</strong> Up to 2 categories and unlimited items per category</li>
          <li><strong>Pro ($29.99/month):</strong> Up to 5 categories and unlimited items per category</li>
          <li><strong>Premium ($49.99/month):</strong> Unlimited categories and items</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">How does the verification system work?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        Customers can enter their collectible's serial number to verify its authenticity. The app checks the serial number against your database and displays the item's details, including name, description, and image. This helps customers confirm they have a genuine collectible from your store.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">Can I upload images for my collectibles?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        Yes! You can upload images for each collectible item. Images are stored securely on Shopify's CDN and can be up to 50MB in size. We support drag-and-drop upload for easy management.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">Can I edit items after creating them?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        Absolutely! You can edit any item's name, serial number, description, status (active/inactive), and upload new images at any time.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">What happens to my data if I uninstall the app?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        If you uninstall the app, all your data (categories, items, verification logs) will be permanently deleted within 48 hours in compliance with GDPR requirements. We recommend exporting any data you want to keep before uninstalling.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">Is my data secure?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        Yes! Your data is stored securely on Amazon Web Services (AWS) infrastructure with industry-standard encryption. We follow Shopify's security best practices and comply with GDPR regulations.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">Can I change my subscription plan?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        Yes, you can upgrade or downgrade your subscription plan at any time from the Billing page in the app. Changes take effect immediately, and you'll be charged or credited on a pro-rata basis.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">Do you offer a free trial?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        Yes! All new users get a 7-day free trial to test the app and see if it fits their needs. No credit card required for the trial period.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">What file formats are supported for images?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        We support all common image formats including JPG, JPEG, PNG, GIF, and WebP. Maximum file size is 50MB per image.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="question">Can customers verify collectibles without an account?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        Yes! Customers can verify collectibles by simply entering the serial number - no account or login required. This makes it easy for anyone to authenticate their collectibles.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="contact-box">
      <h2>Still have questions?</h2>
      <p>Contact our support team at <strong>support@verifymycollectible.com</strong> and we'll be happy to help!</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
